+## gradle-plugins
+
+**High**
+- `components/base/.../dependency/version/MinimumDependencyVersionConventions.kt:18-21` and `BackendSkeletonKotlinJvmConventions.kt:57-63`: `useVersion(minimum)` is applied whenever the coordinates match, without comparing to `requested.version`. So the "minimum" becomes an exact pin. Scenario: a dependency update brings jackson-databind 2.23.0 or netty 4.2.19 into the catalog. Resolution silently downgrades back to 2.22.3 / 4.2.18 while the catalog shows the new version. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: `if (DependencyVersion(requested.version.orEmpty()) < it.minimumVersion) useVersion(...)`.
+- `components/base/.../jib/JibDockerBuildConvention.kt:46-54`: `x.convention(settings.x).convention(default)` replaces the first convention with the default. So the image fingerprint ignores `jvmFlags`, `environment`, `args`, `labels`, `volumes`, `tags` and `reproducibleBuild`. Scenario: changing `jvmFlags` in a service starter rebuilds the image, but `containerBasedServiceTest` and `securityScan` stay UP-TO-DATE and never run against it. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: `x.convention(settings.x.orElse(default))`.
+
+**Medium**
+- `components/base/.../jib/JibDockerBuildConvention.kt:84-85,114,125`: Jib is hardcoded to `nobody` and `OCI`, so the extension's `user` and `imageFormat` settings do nothing. The KDoc says the reproducible-build default is false; the code uses `true`. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: `user = settings.user.getOrElse(defaultUser)` and the same for format; correct the KDoc.
+- `components/base/.../dependency/update/DependencyUpdateConvention.kt:33`: `extension.versionSelector.getOrElse(...)` is read when the plugin is applied, before the consumer's build script configures it, so any value the user sets is ignored. Latent: no consumer sets it today. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: pass a provider/lambda that reads the property lazily (e.g. via `afterEvaluate` or a delegating selector).
+- `components/base/.../dependency/update/UpdateSummaryTask.kt:61,94,188` and `build.gradle.kts:150,173,234`: `project.projectDir` is used at execution time, which breaks the configuration cache. In lattice (cache problems = fail) `updateSummary` fails, and `workspace.sh:530-532` hides that with `2>/dev/null || true`. Confidence: plausible. Fix: capture the directory in a `DirectoryProperty` at configuration time.
+
+**Low**
+- `components/base/.../test/TestTaskConventions.kt:38-41` and `BackendSkeletonKotlinJvmConventions.kt:75-78`: report directories are keyed only by project name. `test`, `containerBasedServiceTest` and `securityScan` in the same project share `build/test-results/test/<name>`. That gives overlapping outputs, which disables caching, and the reports overwrite each other. Confidence: plausible. Fix: include the task name in the path.
+- `components/base/.../maven/publish/MavenPublishConvention.kt:53`: the `doLast` reads `project` at execution time. This is why `publish-if-changed.sh` has to default to `--no-configuration-cache`. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: capture the coordinates string at configuration time, as root `build.gradle.kts:70` already does.
+- `components/base/.../RepositoryConfiguration.kt:36,48-50`: the placeholder repo `https://maven.pkg.github.com/acme/*` is added whenever `GITHUB_USERNAME` and `GITHUB_TOKEN` are set. The token is then sent to a bogus repo and `./gradlew publish` fails. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: only add the repo when an explicit URL property is set.
+- `build.gradle.kts:59-67`: a `<name>-maven` publication is created alongside `java-gradle-plugin`'s `pluginMaven`, with identical coordinates. Every artifact is published twice and Gradle warns about overwrites. Both publication directories exist and are byte-identical. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: drop the manual publication and point `PublicationStateSupport.publicationName` at `pluginMaven`.
+- `components/base/.../dependency/update/UpdateInternalCatalogVersionsTask.kt`: registered in every consumer but never called. Its logic also differs from `update-internal-catalog-versions.sh`, since it ignores `publication-state.properties`. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: delete it.
+- `README.md:28,35,45-57` cites recipes that don't exist (`updateGradle`, `updateDependencies`) and wrong usage coordinates. `IMPROVEMENTS.md` claims there are no plugin IDs and that the configuration cache is off. `build.gradle.kts:164,221` suppresses all wrapper changes and has a dead `extractGradleVersion`. Confidence: confirmed. Fix: update the docs and remove the dead code.
