+# Pillar bug hunt (everything except avro/ and json/)
+
+## web (`modules/web/api/utils`)
+
+**Critical**
+- `filters/correlation/GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:82` together with `GatewayInfoContextParsingFilter.kt:49-51`: a client can supply its own invocation context and the gateway will use it instead of the one it built.
+  - **Why:** the gateway adds its context with `header(...)`, which appends (swissknife `RequestExtensions.kt:6` / `HttpApiDefinition.kt:17`). It never removes a client-sent `x-acme-invocation-context`. The next filter in `GatewayHttpFilter.kt:35-36` joins duplicate headers with `","` and passes the result to `JSONObject(...)`. org.json 20260814 parses the first object and ignores the rest.
+  - **Verified:** http4k keeps the client header first (`[(..., attacker), (..., gateway)]`), and `JSONObject("{\"x\":\"attacker\"},{\"x\":\"gateway\"}")` returns `{"x":"attacker"}`.
+  - **Scenario:** with no bearer token, send `x-acme-invocation-context: {Access.Authenticated, any roles, any customer}`. `toAuthenticated` routes run as that forged user, and `customerOrNull` returns the forged customer.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed (each component tested separately; no end-to-end run).
+  - **Fix:** in `invoke`, `removeHeader(headerNames.correlation.invocationContext)` before `withInvocationContext`, and reject more than one context header instead of joining them.
+
+**High**
+- `GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:93,96,165-168,182-185` (lenses at 201-203): the edge gateway trusts the specified-target-customer, specified-target-tenant, is-test and toggle headers straight from internet clients, with no role check.
+  - **Why it matters:** swissknife `customerOrNull` / `tenantOrNull` prefer `specifiedTargetCustomer` / `specifiedTargetTenant` over the actor's own. Consumers scope SQL by `context.customerOrNull` (element-service-example `PostgresCompliancePlansRepository.kt:42`, `StandardsOperations.kt:60`, `RequirementsOperations.kt:58`).
+  - **Scenario:** any caller, even unauthenticated, sends `x-acme-specified-target-customer-id: <victim org>` and reads or writes that customer's data. Separately, `parseIsTest` takes a client-supplied `isTest=true`, and ignores the header whenever a target customer is set (`customerWithId` always returns `isTest=false`).
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed. `GatewayHttpFilter` itself has no consumers in the two examples.
+  - **Fix:** only honour these headers for actors holding an authorised role (e.g. `admin`/`expert`), and strip them otherwise.
+
+**Medium**
+- `GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:187-191`: JWT audience is never validated.
+  - **Why:** swissknife `newJwtProcessor` calls `setSkipDefaultAudienceValidation()`, and pillar never checks `aud`/`azp` (`targetApplication`).
+  - **Scenario:** a token Keycloak issued to any other client in the same realm is accepted by this API.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** validate `targetApplication.audience`/`authorizedParty` against a configured expected value.
+- `GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:89,105`: issuer selection by domain never works, and the verified-JWT cache ignores the domain.
+  - **Why:** on http4k-jetty, `request.uri.authority` is always `""` (`Uri.of(httpURI.pathQuery + fragment)`, checked in the bytecode), so every request calls `issuerForDomain("")`. The cache is keyed by the token alone.
+  - **Scenario:** if a consumer switches to the Host header, a token verified for realm A is accepted on domain B for up to 30 minutes without re-verification.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** use `Header.HOST` (or explicit config) for the domain, and key the cache by `(domain, token)`.
+- `GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:141-142` (the known TODO, flagged because it has a concrete effect): every authenticated `UserAccount` gets `tenant = Example.tenant` (`example.com`), not `Acme.tenant`.
+  - **Scenario:** `tenantOrNull` puts all real users in the `example.com` tenant, so tenant scoping is wrong. All customers are also `isTest=false`, so test-customer traffic is treated as production.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** take the tenant (and customer lookup) from injected configuration or a function.
+
+**Low**
+- `GatewayInvocationContextFilter.kt:194`: every failure, including an expired or invalid JWT, becomes a 400 with the raw exception message in the reason phrase.
+  - **Scenario:** clients don't refresh their token because they never see a 401. jose4j messages echo token claims into the status line.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** map JWT verification failures to 401 with a fixed message.
+- `GatewayInfoContextParsingFilter.kt:49`: the header name is compared case-sensitively (`it.first == ...`), unlike http4k lenses.
+  - **Scenario:** a hop that forwards `X-Acme-Invocation-Context` over HTTP/1.1 (Jetty keeps the case of custom headers) means the context is ignored and `toAuthenticated` fails with a 400 lens failure.
+  - **Confidence:** plausible.
+  - **Fix:** `it.first.equals(name, ignoreCase = true)`.
+
