+## modulith-example bug hunt (read-only)
+
+### payment-command-endpoint
+
+- **High** — `content/modules/payment-command-endpoint/module/implementation/.../PaymentCommandEndpointModule.kt:30-33` — The production module is wired to `StubbedSendPaymentProcessingResultSubscriber`, which returns `ProcessedSuccessfully` after `delay(2.seconds)` no matter what. Balance and account existence are never checked.
+  - **Scenario:** a payment from an empty or nonexistent account gets HTTP 200 with `{"type":"processed-successfully","was-processed":true}`. README:62 and README:71 say the client is told when a payment is rejected.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** until the NATS reply exists, return an "accepted / pending" result instead of claiming it was processed.
+
+- **High** — `content/modules/payment-command-endpoint/application/model/.../ApplicationImplementation.kt:25-34` — Nothing checks that the authenticated actor owns `sourceAccount`. `toAuthenticated` only checks that the caller is authenticated.
+  - **Scenario:** any authenticated user can send a payment debiting someone else's account. README:16 says operations are only allowed for the account owner.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** compare the actor's account in `InvocationContext` with `arguments.sourceAccount` and return an `ApiError` (403/422) if they differ.
+
+- **Medium** — `.../ApplicationImplementation.kt:39,32` plus `SendPaymentCommandEndpoint.kt:33` — Each request gets a fresh event id, and the event is published before the endpoint waits for the result.
+  - **Scenario:** after 10s `withTimeout` throws. `CatchAndLogErrors` turns that into a plain-text 500, but the command is already on Pulsar. The client retries and a second command with a different id is published, so the payment is applied twice once the processor exists.
+  - **Confidence:** the timeout-to-500 path is confirmed; the double-apply is plausible.
+  - **Fix:** take a client idempotency key, derive the event id from it, and map a timeout to 202 or 504 with the command id.
+
+- **Low** — `.../StubbedSendPaymentProcessingResultSubscriber.kt:12-20` — The `CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob())` is never cancelled when the module stops. If `awaitResult` throws, the `CompletableDeferred` is never completed.
+  - **Scenario:** the request hangs for the full 10s timeout, then returns 500. Pending coroutines keep running after `stop()`.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** return `scope.async { awaitResult() }` directly and cancel the scope on module stop.
+
+- **Low** — `.../endpoint/SendPaymentCommandEndpoint.kt:28` (same bug at `deposit-event-endpoint/.../DepositEventEndpoint.kt:25`) — The log line uses `$arguments` before the local variable is declared, so it resolves to the companion's body lens.
+  - **Scenario:** every request logs the lens's `toString()` instead of the request arguments.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** move the log line after `val arguments = arguments(request)`.
+
+- **Low (test)** — `.../module/test/specification/PaymentCommandEndpointModuleTestSpecification.kt:53-54` — Only the status code is asserted; the response body is never checked.
+  - **Scenario:** the always-success stub (first finding) passes the module and service tests unnoticed.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** assert the deserialized `ApplicationResult`.
+
+### deposit-event-endpoint
+
+- **High** — `content/modules/deposit-event-endpoint/adapters/driving/http/endpoint/.../DepositEventEndpoint.kt:23` plus `application/model/.../ApplicationImplementation.kt:16` — Any authenticated actor, including the ordinary `user` role, can post a deposit to any account. The event's id, timestamp and `context.invocation` come from the request body and are published unchanged.
+  - **Scenario:** an account holder credits their own account and forges the actor and trace recorded on the event. The module test even asserts the client-supplied context is kept (`DepositEventEndpointModuleTestSpecification.kt:65`).
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** require a system/integration role, and build the event metadata from the request's `InvocationContext` (keep the external id as a data field).
+
+### account-event-processor
+
+- **High** — `content/modules/account-event-processor/application/model/.../Application.kt:39-64` — Every handler body is a TODO. `processAsCompositeEvent` (swissknife) returns `Success` for an empty lambda.
+  - **Scenario:** the module is not wired into the service at all: there is no dependency in `content/service/starter/build.gradle.kts:27-28`, it is missing from the module set in `Service.kt:51-56`, and from `ModulesTestSpecification`. If it were wired as-is, every deposit and payment would be acknowledged as processed and silently dropped.
+  - **Docs impact:** README:68-72 lists it as "Done", including the insufficient-balance and same-account rejections.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
+  - **Fix:** move it to "To Do" in the README; don't wire it until the handlers either do the work or return a failure.
+
+### shared
+
+- **High (latent)** — `content/shared/account/domain/model/.../AccountEventDataExtensions.kt:9` — `OutboundPayment.inbound()` swaps the two accounts: `InboundPayment(targetAccount = sourceAccount, sourceAccount = targetAccount, ...)`.
+  - **Scenario:** a payment A→B produces an inbound event that credits A (the payer) back and is keyed to A's partition. B is never credited. It currently has no callers.
+  - **Confidence:** confirmed.
