+
+**Low**
+- `content/shared/compliance/plan/domain/model/.../requirement/standard/Standard.kt:17-20` and `Clause.kt:10`: `compareTo` uses only reference and date (Clause adds name), which is inconsistent with data-class `equals` (edition, language, format, type). Clauses from different editions compare equal, which breaks any `TreeSet`/`sortedSetOf` and gives ambiguous ordering. Confirmed. Fix: extend the comparator to every field `equals` uses.
+- `content/shared/compliance/plan/domain/model/.../standard/Standard.kt:92`: `Submission.shortName` is `null`, while its companion defines `"510(k)"`. Confirmed but currently unused. Fix: `override val shortName: Name get() = Companion.shortName`.
+- `content/shared/compliance/plan/domain/model/.../market/Market.kt`, `.../organization/StandardsDevelopingOrganization.kt`: these take any `Name`, but the Avro schemas encode them as closed enums (`MarketCode`, `StandardsDevelopingOrganizationCode`). A non-listed code builds a valid domain object, then throws on publish. Confirmed. Fix: make them enums, or validate in `init`.
+- `.../avro/standard/organization/OrganizationAvroSchemas.kt:12`: `all = sequenceOf(code, code)` omits `standardsDevelopingOrganization`; `.../avro/standard/device/DeviceAvroSchemas.kt:14` omits `wholeDeviceCode`. The schema container tests never load those schemas directly. Confirmed. Fix: list each schema once.
+- `content/migrator/postgres/domain/src/main/kotlin/Serialization.kt:11`: `writeRaw` skips Jackson's separator/colon bookkeeping. It works today only because `Standard`/`Requirement` are serialized at the JSON root. Nesting them in a field or list would emit invalid JSON. Plausible (latent). Fix: `writeRawValue`.
